can see their paper for a

00:31:57.701 --> 00:31:59.891
more formal treatment.

00:32:00.481 --> 00:32:02.961
So suppose we're moving through weight space and we're oscillating

00:32:02.961 --> 00:32:04.821
along the top eigenvector of the Hessian.

00:32:04.991 --> 00:32:06.591
Which is like the vertical direction here.

00:32:08.031 --> 00:32:09.961
So let w star

00:32:10.521 --> 00:32:12.941
denote the point where you'd be if we if we were not oscillating.

00:32:13.750 --> 00:32:15.910
And let w denote the point where you'd

00:32:15.911 --> 00:32:18.051
be where we are because we are oscillating.

00:32:18.451 --> 00:32:20.770
So in other words, because we're oscillating,

00:32:21.101 --> 00:32:22.960
we're displaced from w star

00:32:23.481 --> 00:32:25.671
along the u direction by some magnitude.

00:32:25.831 --> 00:32:27.011
Let's call that x.

00:32:27.981 --> 00:32:30.090
So how does the gradient where we are

00:32:30.891 --> 00:32:33.031
w star plus x u, relate to the gradient

00:32:33.031 --> 00:32:35.131
at w star is

00:32:35.131 --> 00:32:36.710
where we'd be if we were not oscillating.

00:32:38.301 --> 00:32:40.161
So by Taylor expand let's let's do

00:32:40.461 --> 00:32:42.141
Taylor expansion. Gonna tailor expand Noblal

00:32:42.661 --> 00:32:44.770
the gradient map around w

00:32:44.770 --> 00:32:46.840
star. So

00:32:47.411 --> 00:32:49.771
okay. First term is not very interesting, just gradient

00:32:49.831 --> 00:32:52.101
w star. Next term,

00:32:53.141 --> 00:32:55.210
which is first order in the gradient or second order

00:32:55.210 --> 00:32:57.381
in the loss, says that the gradient

00:32:57.381 --> 00:32:59.451
w star plus x u has a term that

00:32:59.451 --> 00:33:01.371
is like Hessian at w star,

00:33:01.471 --> 00:33:03.740
times x u. That should make sense

00:33:03.740 --> 00:33:05.481
because the Heshn is the derivative of the gradient.

00:33:08.441 --> 00:33:10.521
But we can simplify that further because

00:33:10.521 --> 00:33:12.291
u is an eigenvector of the Hessian,

00:33:12.530 --> 00:33:14.501
particular, it's an eigen value eigenvector

00:33:14.901 --> 00:33:16.601
whose eigenvalue is s, the sharpness,

00:33:16.951 --> 00:33:19.031
So Heshin times u is just sharpness times

00:33:19.031 --> 00:33:21.381
u. And sharpness

00:33:21.381 --> 00:33:23.121
is a scalar. So this is a

00:33:23.601 --> 00:33:25.311
vector that's pointing in the u direction.

00:33:25.791 --> 00:33:27.951
And when we follow the negative gradient, this

00:33:27.951 --> 00:33:30.161
term's gonna send us into the minus

00:33:30.161 --> 00:33:32.261
u direction. So this is just the term that's causing

00:33:32.261 --> 00:33:34.461
the oscillations. As we already

00:33:34.461 --> 00:33:36.641
expected The magic

00:33:36.711 --> 00:33:38.861
quote unquote, is coming from

00:33:38.861 --> 00:33:41.110
the next term, in the Taylor expansion of

00:33:41.111 --> 00:33:43.340
the gradient. So the next

00:33:43.340 --> 00:33:45.391
term looks like this, me unpack

00:33:45.391 --> 00:33:47.521
it. This is the curvature in

00:33:47.521 --> 00:33:49.661
the u direction. U transpose hessian

00:33:49.661 --> 00:33:51.841
u. This is the gradient of

00:33:51.841 --> 00:33:53.961
that. So the gradient of the curvature in the

00:33:53.961 --> 00:33:56.391
u direction. The curvature

00:33:56.451 --> 00:33:58.611
in the u direction well, because you as a top

00:33:59.091 --> 00:34:01.180
eigenvector of the Hessian, this is just the top

00:34:01.181 --> 00:34:03.431
eigenvalue of the Hessian. Or the

00:34:03.431 --> 00:34:05.441
sharpness. And moreover, you can

00:34:05.441 --> 00:34:07.141
show that the grading of the curvature

00:34:07.801 --> 00:34:10.120
e, e, direction, is just the gradient of

00:34:10.121 --> 00:34:10.621
the sharpness.

00:34:12.414 --> 00:34:14.565
In other words, just by

00:34:14.565 --> 00:34:16.749
tailor expanding, we see that the gradient at w star

00:34:16.749 --> 00:34:18.958
plus x u contains the

00:34:18.959 --> 00:34:20.749
term that is proportional

00:34:21.309 --> 00:34:22.459
to the grading of the sharpness.

00:34:23.819 --> 00:34:26.138
Thus, when we take a negative gradient

00:34:26.139 --> 00:34:27.928
step at w star plus x u,

00:34:28.489 --> 00:34:30.499
it's gonna automatically take

00:34:30.499 --> 00:34:32.839
a negative gradient step on the sharpness.

00:34:33.888 --> 00:34:36.128
And the step size, quote unquote, of this

00:34:36.129 --> 00:34:38.359
negative gradient step is one

00:34:38.499 --> 00:34:40.939
half eta x squared where remember that x

00:34:40.999 --> 00:34:42.869
squared is the squared magnitude of the oscillation.

00:34:43.529 --> 00:34:45.659
So the larger the oscillation, the stronger the

00:34:46.059 --> 00:34:47.599
implicit gradient step on the sharpness.

00:34:49.059 --> 00:34:50.599
So in other words,

00:34:51.419 --> 00:34:53.579
we already knew that sharpness generates

00:34:53.579 --> 00:34:55.719
oscillations. But

00:34:55.719 --> 00:34:57.829
now what we see from this third order expansion

00:34:57.829 --> 00:35:00.049
is that there's also an arrow in the other

00:35:00.049 --> 00:35:02.239
