bits. So we have inputs

01:01:07.546 --> 01:01:09.576
our training bits, bits, sorry, bit strings.

01:01:10.216 --> 01:01:12.346
And then in the training data, we have a mixture

01:01:12.666 --> 01:01:15.166
Either we have, long demonstrations,

01:01:16.316 --> 01:01:18.546
where we have these bits of input, and

01:01:18.546 --> 01:01:20.626
then we have these partial parities. You see

01:01:20.626 --> 01:01:22.966
this there on the bottom line of this blue yellow

01:01:23.036 --> 01:01:25.096
red. So, we have the blue input, It's

01:01:25.096 --> 01:01:26.636
a string of zero ones.

01:01:27.126 --> 01:01:29.155
And then the yellow bits there are

01:01:29.156 --> 01:01:31.235
partial parities, so the parity of the first bit,

01:01:31.235 --> 01:01:33.454
the parity of the first and the second bit, the first second

01:01:33.454 --> 01:01:35.566
third, and so on. Is how you would compute

01:01:35.566 --> 01:01:37.805
parity probably. Right? You would go along the

01:01:37.806 --> 01:01:39.966
chain, compute the partial parities. I mean,

01:01:39.966 --> 01:01:42.046
how else can you do it? Right? And then, the red is the

01:01:42.046 --> 01:01:44.186
output bit. So what we what we'll

01:01:44.186 --> 01:01:46.326
have is training a training mixture

01:01:46.326 --> 01:01:48.515
for a small transformer which

01:01:48.516 --> 01:01:50.615
is a lot of these short answer

01:01:50.676 --> 01:01:52.325
parities and

01:01:52.886 --> 01:01:55.046
a a few, a fraction, which we call

01:01:55.046 --> 01:01:56.826
p of chain of thought, p code,

01:01:57.056 --> 01:01:59.266
of these long demonstrations. And

01:01:59.266 --> 01:02:01.585
what you need to know about parity is usually one, you know, in

01:02:01.585 --> 01:02:03.596
theoretical computer science, it's always used

01:02:04.156 --> 01:02:06.266
as prototypical hard problem. It's hard.

01:02:06.426 --> 01:02:08.606
Parity is not so easy. To

01:02:08.606 --> 01:02:10.685
do, you know. Whereas, if you have this

01:02:10.686 --> 01:02:12.735
long chain of thought, and you just follow

01:02:12.736 --> 01:02:14.766
it along and you reason this way, then

01:02:14.766 --> 01:02:17.016
it becomes easy. Right? So, this is

01:02:17.016 --> 01:02:19.176
our training mix. So, we use this dataset that

